FADE IN:

EXT. STEALTH CARRIER - SPACE - NIGHT

BLACK.

The soft mechanical INHALE of a pressurized bay. A sound like breathing machinery.

The darkness resolves. A stealth carrier skims just below orbit—lights killed, hull freezing in the void. The ship is all angles and shadow, a predator in the deep.

INT. STEALTH CARRIER - BAY - CONTINUOUS

Seven agents kneel in formation. Helmets cradled in gloved hands. Eyes forward. Motionless as statues.

Their pulse nodes blink in perfect unison—a quiet metronome counting down to something inevitable.

BAEBE (20s, cybernetically enhanced, precise) rises from a monk-still crouch. The faint blue glow at her throat pulses once. No tremor. No doubt.

She studies the city's distant lattice through a narrow viewport—a circuit board someone is playing in real time. Lights pulse and flow like data streams.

FLIGHT COMMS (V.O.)
(hushed, filtered)
Ghost mode engaged.

Silence. The agents don't move. They're already gone.

BAEBE
(whisper)
You fall faster than the feed can follow. That's how you stay clean.

COMMAND (V.O.)
(dry, metallic)
Execute.

The ramp IRISES OPEN. The sound is organic, almost biological.

The Earth curves below—silent and impossibly close. A blue marble wrapped in cloud.

EXT. SPACE - CONTINUOUS

Each agent steps out onto a thin disc that ERUPTS INTO PLASMA, then disintegrates beneath their boots.

Human meteors cut the stratosphere—searing tracer lines the color of welding arcs. They fall like shooting stars.

BAEBE'S POV - FALLING

The heads-up display snaps to life on her visor:

SUPER: TARGET: T-ALPHA
SUPER: ALTITUDE: 87,000 FT
SUPER: DESCENDING

Her pulse node flickers once—blue... then something else. A micro-Resonant Fade flutters around her—the edges of her form warping as if the world lags a frame.

She blinks. The glitch resolves.

The city rushes up. An 800-story glass monolith sings with low frequency light—a beacon in the dark.

EXT. TOWER - CONTINUOUS

The squad angles toward the structure. Plasma trails converge.

FADE TO BLACK.
